INT. NIGHT COURT - ARRAIGNMENT ROOM - 1 A.M.

A drab room under buzzing fluorescents. A raised bench, a witness stand with a chipped rail, a row of empty gallery seats. A clock stuck at ten past three.

JUDGE OCTAVIA ROSENBLATT-ODUYA, sixties, sits at the bench with a thermos. At the defense table, PUBLIC DEFENDER LEON FAIRWEATHER, thirties, shuffles papers that do not need shuffling. At the prosecution table, ASSISTANT DA MERCEDES IBARRA-NOLAN, forties, taps a pen. In the dock stands a MAN in a green hospital gown, barefoot, tall, hair sticking up.

JUDGE ROSENBLATT-ODUYA
(to the room)
We're on the record. Docket 4471. State versus...

She squints at her papers.

JUDGE ROSENBLATT-ODUYA (CONT'D)
(to herself)
John Doe? Again?

LEON
Your Honor, my client has declined to give his name.

MAN
It's not that I decline. I'm not certain.

JUDGE ROSENBLATT-ODUYA
Mr. Doe, do you understand the charge?

MAN
Trespassing at the aquarium.

MERCEDES
After hours. In the shark tank.

MAN
It was a very peaceful tank.

LEON
(to the Man, low)
Please don't talk.

MERCEDES
(to the judge)
The State will note he also had a crowbar and a wetsuit.

LEON
It was a diving lesson.

MERCEDES
At two in the morning.

MAN
(muttering)
I was looking for someone.

JUDGE ROSENBLATT-ODUYA
Looking for whom?

MAN
A woman. Long hair. She said her name was Marisol and that she lived in the tank.

Leon closes his eyes. Mercedes sets down her pen. The judge puts a hand over her mouth to cover a smile.

JUDGE ROSENBLATT-ODUYA
Mr. Doe...

MAN
It's not Doe. I remember now. It's Corwin.

LEON
(whispering)
Corwin?

CORWIN
Corwin Albright-Santos. I'm a marine biologist.

MERCEDES
(to the judge)
Your Honor, he's been in the system four times this year.

CORWIN
Five.

LEON
Corwin, please.

JUDGE ROSENBLATT-ODUYA
Mr. Albright-Santos, I'm going to release you on your own recognizance. On one condition.

CORWIN
Anything.

JUDGE ROSENBLATT-ODUYA
Stay out of the tank.

CORWIN
(after a long pause)
I'll try.

She bangs the gavel. The clock still reads ten past three.
